              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-construction" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+presheaf"} small presheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
            (only) up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            that is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategorical"} bicategorical
            in nature. However, it is also possible to give a description of the free
            %em strict
            cocompletion, i.e. one satisfying a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-categorical
            universal property, in the sense of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+of+categories"} isomorphism of categories
          %p
            Explicitly, the small presheaf construction exhibits a left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoadjoint"} pseudoadjoint
            to the forgetful 2-functor from the 2-category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small"} locally small
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+categories"} cocomplete categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-adjoint"} strict 2-adjoint
            (or left
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %p
            Abstractly, this follows by the results of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KellyLack2000"} Kelly and Lack (2000)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Ehresmann1981"} Ehresmann (1981)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BPG2021"} Beurier, Pastor &amp; Guitart (2021)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
            whose objects are not presheaves, but simply
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
            %strong atlases
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Ehresmann1981"} Ehresmann (1981)
            %strong clusters
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EV1987"} Ehresmann and Vanbremeersch (1987)
            %strong category of clusters
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Clu
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Clu(\mathscr{C})
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BPG2021"} Beurier, Pastor, and Guitart (2021)
          %p
            The morphisms can be seen to satisfy the
            %strong limit–colimit formula
            (
            %a{:href => "#BPG2021"}> Beurier–Pastor–Guitart
            , Proposition 3.11): given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒫
                  %mo →
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \colon \mathscr{P} \to \mathscr{C}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒬
                    %mo →
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \colon \mathscr{Q} \to \mathscr{C}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Clu
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≅
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi.mathscript 𝒫
                    %msub
                      %mi colim
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi.mathscript 𝒬
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Clu(\mathscr{C})(P, Q) \,\cong\, lim_{p \in \mathscr{P}} colim_{q \in \mathscr{Q}} \mathscr{C}\big(P(p), Q(q)\big)
          %p
            The category of clusters embeds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithfully"} fully faithfully
            into the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+presheaf+category"} small presheaf category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LClu
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LClu(\mathscr{C})
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BPG2021"} Beurier, Pastor &amp; Guitart (2021)
          %p
            That the category of clusters forms the free strict cocompletion was stated in
            %a{:href => "#Ehresmann1981"} Ehresmann (1981)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#EV1987"} Ehresmann and Vanbremeersch (1987)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BPG2021"} Beurier, Pastor &amp;Guitart (2021)
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Ehresmann1981"} Ehresmann (1981)
            also considers the restriction to the free strict cocompletion under a specified class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{J}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            shapes: this is given by restricting the objects of the category of clusters.
          %h2#universal_property Universal property
          %p
            See
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BPG2021"} Beurier–Pastor–Guitart
          %p
            Consider a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %mo =
                  %mi Clu
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{F}=Clu(\mathscr{C})
            (as desribed above), and the canonical inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %mi Clu
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\colon\mathscr{C}\to Clu(\mathscr{C})
            that sends an object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
            to a diagram indexed by the terminal category. The triple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathscr{C},\mathscr{F},I)
            has the following additional canonical structure: for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+diagram"} small diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒫
                  %mo →
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\colon\mathscr{P}\to\mathscr{C}
            we have a canonical colimit cocone
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi λ
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi I
                  %mi P
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda^P\colon I P\Rightarrow \lambda(I P)
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{F}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda(I P)
            is an object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{F}
            given by the diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            itself, interpreted as an object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{F}
          %p
            The free strict cocompletion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Clu
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Clu(\mathscr{C})
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
            satisfies the following universal property: given another such triple
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℱ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi I
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathscr{F}',I',\lambda')
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I'\colon \mathscr{C}\to\mathscr{F}'
            is a functor landing in a locally small cocomplete category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{F}'
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda'
            is a choice of a colimit cocone for every diagram of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ′
                  %mi P
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I' P'
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒫
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P'\colon \mathscr{P}'\to \mathscr{C}
            ), there is a unique functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %mo →
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\colon\mathscr{F}\to\mathscr{F}'
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mi I
                  %mo =
                  %mi I
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J I = I'
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            sends cocones in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            to the corresponding cocones in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda'
          %p
            In particular,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{F}
            is unique up to an isomorphism.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            The assignment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi Clu
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}\mapsto Clu(\mathscr{C})
            yields a
            %strong strict
            2-functor from locally small categories to locally small categories that implements the free cocompletion construction.
          %p
            This stands in contrast to the usual construction of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+presheaves"} small presheaves
          %p
            By restricting the types of diagrams in the construction of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Clu
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Clu(\mathscr{C})
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-completions"} ind-completions
